  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1/3: Fixed 5 failing assertions (min_leq_max, clear_initializes_min_max, reset_reinitializes_min_max, normal_update_tracks_sup_inf, liveness_max_min_update_next_cycle). Root cause: all 5 are assertion_timing/assertion_gating errors where assertions checked register values in the wrong cycle or unconditionally. Changes: (1) min_leq_max: gated with normal_update instead of unconditional fvAssert; (2) clear_initializes_min_max: added RegNext on antecedent to check cycle-after-clear; (3) reset_reinitializes_min_max: removed RegNext on consequent to check post-update register values; (4) normal_update_tracks_sup_inf: added RegNext(normal_update) antecedent and prev_sup/prev_inf shadow registers; (5) liveness_max_min_update_next_cycle: replaced max===sup/min===inf with max===prev_sup/min===prev_inf using shadow registers. All assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
    "Repair round 2/3: Fixed 3 remaining failing assertions (min_leq_max, normal_update_tracks_sup_inf, liveness_max_min_update_next_cycle). Root cause: all three fail at cycle 0 because sentinel register initial values (min=0xFFFF...FFFF, max=0) violate the expected register-relationship assertions, and formal tools may treat RegNext initial values as nondeterministic. Fix: (1) Added `notFirstCycle = RegNext(true.B, false.B)` guard register. (2) min_leq_max: gated with `&& notFirstCycle` to skip cycle-0 sentinel mismatch. (3) normal_update_tracks_sup_inf: gated with `&& notFirstCycle` to skip initial-state min/prev_inf mismatch. (4) liveness_max_min_update_next_cycle: replaced `assertNextStepWhen(normal_update, ...)` with `assertImplies(RegNext(normal_update) && notFirstCycle, ...)` to match the correct single-register pattern and avoid double-registering semantics. All assertion labels preserved unchanged. Homologous assertions: normal_update_tracks_sup_inf and liveness_max_min_update_next_cycle are structurally identical after this fix.",
    "Repair round 3/3: Fixed remaining failing assertion min_leq_max. Root cause: assertion timing error — when transitioning from idle (io_enable=0) to active (io_enable=1), min/max registers still hold stale sentinel values (min=0xFFFF...FFFF, max=0) at the moment normal_update becomes true. The registers are updated during the same cycle via non-blocking assignments, but min_leq_max checks immediately. Fix: changed antecedent from `normal_update && notFirstCycle` to `RegNext(normal_update) && notFirstCycle`, so the assertion checks one cycle after normal_update fires, when registers have taken their new values. This is consistent with how Safety 4 (normal_update_tracks_sup_inf) and Liveness 12 (liveness_max_min_update_next_cycle) are already written. Assertion label `min_leq_max` preserved unchanged. No homologous assertions found — this is the only assertion that used `normal_update` (without RegNext) to guard a register-value check."
